  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Send a Child in Aleppo to School for a Year</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project focuses on providing literacy and quality education for 100 disadvantaged girls and boys affected by war and ever-growing poverty in Aleppo, Syria. At-risk young people attending public schools, and vocational or university courses, are funded and mentored to ensure school retention, literacy and future livelihood. Today, 86% of Syrian live below the poverty line. Even if public education is free, it is out of reach for many. Through your support, we can give Aleppo children hope.</narrative>
  </description>
